# Which secret each application reads from Vault, and from which KV v2 entry.
#
#   <entry> <NAME>
#
# entry is the KV v2 entry under secret/: `shared` is read by every application, any other entry
# only by the application of that name. Every entry other than `shared` is an application: it gets
# its own AppRole and a read-only policy for `secret/data/shared` and `secret/data/<entry>`.
# Vault policies cannot grant part of an entry, so a name goes to `shared` only when every
# application uses it.
#
# NAME is both the key inside the entry and the file name Vault Agent renders under /run/secrets.
#
# scripts/vault-lib.sh derives from this file the policies (written once, when Vault is first
# initialized) and each agent's configuration (rendered every time the agent starts). README.md
# covers adding a secret later.

app      API_KEY
postgres POSTGRES_PASSWORD
